<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">
<!--
  @decision DEC-PHASE13-058
  @category SECURITY
  @title The Cockpit installs and removes optional tools through one pinned polkit action, with the password remembered for about five minutes
  @status accepted
  @rationale #198. The Cockpit runs as the desktop user; orionx-optional needs
    root. pkexec 126, polkitd 126 and the mate-polkit agent are in the image
    (live/filesystem.packages of v3.1.6), and the agent autostarts under XFCE
    (NotShowIn=GNOME;KDE;). The owner allowed a cached password only if simple
    and secure (2026-11-25): auth_admin_keep is polkit's own cache, one word
    here and no code of ours; it lasts about five minutes and covers only this
    action, for the process that authenticated, in the active local session.
    Inactive and remote sessions get no. exec.path pins the one program, and
    the helper accepts only `install|uninstall ID` with ID from the catalogue,
    so this action cannot run anything else. Recorded, not changed here: the
    live account also has NOPASSWD sudo (live-config default), so this prompt
    confirms the operator's intent rather than separating privilege; #203 is
    that decision. Amended 2026-11-27, measured on the v3.2.0 image: live-config
    also installs /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/sudo_on_live.rules, which returns
    YES for every action of the live user in an active local session, and
    rules override these defaults. pkcheck authorizes this action for
    orionx-operator with no prompt (exit 0). auth_admin_keep therefore applies
    only to other accounts, or once #203 removes that rule; the Cockpit and the
    User Guide say so instead of promising a prompt.
-->
<policyconfig>
  <vendor>Orion-X Phoenix Edition</vendor>
  <action id="org.orionx.optional.manage">
    <description>Install or remove an Orion-X optional tool</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to install or remove an optional tool</message>
    <icon_name>system-software-install</icon_name>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin_keep</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/opt/orionx/scripts/optional/orionx-optional</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
